<figure class="figure">
<p><img src="https://benjaminhan.net/posts/20210118-end-to-end-re-comparisons/cover.jpg" class="img-fluid figure-img"></p>
<figcaption>Stop incorrect comparisons in end-to-end RE. Image from <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.10684">arXiv</a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
<p>Bruno Taillé, Vincent Guigue, Geoffrey Scoutheeten and patrick gallinari asked these important questions:</p>
<ul>
<li>What are we measuring?</li>
<li>What are we comparing to?</li>
<li>What are not explicated in the literature?</li>
</ul>
<p>We should have more papers like this!</p>
<p>Let’s Stop Incorrect Comparisons in End-to-end Relation Extraction! <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.10684" class="uri">https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.10684</a></p>
